## Tab 3: Practice

**Mental model:** "How my practice measures success"

This merges Practice Goals + Thresholds, deduplicates the note deadline conflict, and organizes everything by *what you're measuring* rather than *goal vs threshold* (a distinction our audience doesn't care about).

### Layout

**Header area:**

- Title: "Practice Settings"
- Subtitle: "Goals, definitions, and how metrics are calculated"
- Right side: "Save Changes" button (appears only when dirty, emerald gradient with check icon)

**Main content: Stacked sections, not a grid of cards**

The current Practice Goals uses a 2x2 card grid, and Thresholds uses another set of cards. This creates a lot of visual noise. Instead: clean stacked sections with clear dividers.

### Section 1: Practice Goals

Two goal inputs side by side:

```
+--------------------+  +--------------------+
|  Monthly Revenue   |  |  Target Rebook     |
|     $125,000       |  |       90%          |
|  $1.5M/year        |  |  Industry: 85%     |
+--------------------+  +--------------------+
```

Each is a `ConfigCard` with:

- Icon + label at top
- Large inline-editable value (Tiempos Headline serif, big)
- Contextual subtext (annual projection, industry benchmark)

**Note: Sessions and Clients goals are NOT here.** These are computed from individual clinician goals (set in the Clinicians tab). A read-only summary appears below:

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Team Goals: 160 sessions/wk  •  225 clients                    │
│  Based on 5 clinicians → Edit individual goals in Clinicians tab │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Clicking "Edit individual goals" navigates to the Clinicians tab.

### Section 2: Client & Session Rules

Combined section for all client and session configuration:

**Churn Definition**

One simple input: "A client is considered churned after [X] days without an appointment."

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Days until churned: [90]                              │
│  Clients with no appointment in 90+ days are churned   │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**At-Risk Thresholds**

Three color-coded cards: Low Risk (X days), Medium Risk (X days), High Risk (X days). Keep current visual design - the colored cards work well.

**Session Rules**

Two settings side by side:

```
+--------------------+  +--------------------+
|  Late Cancel       |  |  Note Deadline     |
|  Window            |  |                    |
|    24 hours        |  |    48 hours        |
|  before appt       |  |  after session     |
+--------------------+  +--------------------+
```

Note deadline uses button selector (24h / 48h / 72h / 96h) - more friendly than freeform input.

### The Flow

```
Owner opens Practice tab
  -> Sees Revenue goal and Rebook Rate at the top
  -> Notices team session/client totals below (read-only, links to Clinicians)
  -> Scrolls to Client & Session Rules
  -> Notices note deadline is 72h, wants to tighten to 48h
  -> Clicks 48h button -> button highlights -> "Save Changes" appears top-right
  -> Clicks Save -> done
```

**Why this is better:** Practice-level settings are minimal and focused. Session/client goals are clearly tied to individual clinicians (where they belong). Two sections instead of five.

